This "minishell" was a project intended to famialiarize myself more with the innerworkings of a shell. It features a few custom command implementations, uses exec to do the remainder, implements an interupt handler for SIGINT (ctrl + C), and features some error handling.

Custom commands are as follows: (Attempting to input too few or two many arguments will result in an error)
* cd [directory] - changes the current directory to [directory]. A ~ will expand to your home directory! 
* pwd - prints the current working directory
* lf - lists every file and directory in your current working directory, excluding those that start with . or ..
* lp - lists all currently running processes by reading /proc sorted by their PID! Owner, and the command from cmdline are also listed. 
* exit - exits minishell

